      "reason": "stored_sessions was the count of puts clamped to the cache's capacity, but resumptions take sessions out, so occupancy was overstated and heap_per_stored_session understated. The server now counts the sessions the cache holds as it follows the cache's rules (a put adds one, a take that finds its key removes one, an insertion that fills the order queue evicts one) and records the cache's preallocation. The rows with stateless tickets do not depend on it and are from the original run."
    }
